Injection points for the port's tests, at eleven of Apache Cloudberry's
faults inside PostgreSQL's own code, under their own names, which its
isolation2 tests set (src/test/isolation2/sql): an insert into a table,
which pg_terminate_backend holds in a loop; a backend about to read its
next command, which check_gxid fails the coordinator at; the lookup of a
collation's locale, which gp_collation fails on a segment, as of a locale
it lacks; a scan, which orphan_temp_table fails a segment in; REINDEX
DATABASE before it looks for its tables, and a relation's REINDEX once its
indexes are rebuilt, which reindex holds while another session drops a
table or makes an index; CREATE INDEX before it locks its table, which
concurrent_index_creation_should_not_deadlock holds two sessions at;
VACUUM FULL once the relation's files are swapped, which
vacuum_full_interrupt cancels it at; a BRIN scan's page added to its
bitmap, which brin_heap counts, and the summary of a BRIN index's last,
partial range, which it holds while the table grows; and a base backup
once its checkpoint is made, which master_wal_switch holds while the
coordinator switches to a new WAL file and checkpoints:

  heap_insert                         heapam.c, heap_insert()
  before_read_command                 postgres.c, ReadCommand()
  collate_locale_os_lookup            pg_locale.c, pg_newlocale_from_collation()
  before_exec_scan                    execProcnode.c, ExecProcNodeFirst()
  reindex_db                          indexcmds.c, ReindexMultipleTables()
  reindex_relation                    index.c, reindex_relation()
  defineindex_before_acquire_lock     indexcmds.c, DefineIndex()
  after_swap_relation_files           repack.c, finish_heap_swap()
  brin_bitmap_page_added              brin.c, bringetbitmap()
  summarize_last_partial_range        brin.c, summarize_range()
  base_backup_post_create_checkpoint  basebackup.c, perform_base_backup()

Most are where Cloudberry's are.  heap_insert gives its callback the
table's name, as Cloudberry's call does, for a test sets the fault for one
table.  Cloudberry asks for before_exec_scan at each row its ExecScan()
fetches, which PostgreSQL 19 inlines in every scan (ExecScanExtended());
this point is a scan node's first execution, once for each, so that the
tests' build looks for no attached point at each row a scan returns.
PostgreSQL 19 rebuilds a relation's TOAST table's indexes before its own,
where Cloudberry's REINDEX rebuilt them after, its fault between the two:
reindex_relation is after the relation's own.  And the base backup's point
is inside its error cleanup, so that a backup a test fails there is ended
as any other failed one is.

gp_core's fault injector attaches a fault of Cloudberry's name to the point
(gp_fault.c), heap_insert's with a line in its fault_points that says the
point gives the table's name.  They serve tests alone, so they are not in
the core series: Dockerfile.pg applies this after
test-injection-points.patch, to the tree of either ref, vanilla or
patched, so that the two images still differ only in the ref.  Dormant, as
any point is: without injection points the macro is empty, and with them a
point nothing attached to runs no callback.

